  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Democratic Dialogues for Progressive Taxation to Tackle Inequality in Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the project is to work with implementing partners as well as strategic partners in the media and labour unions to push for progressive and gender sensitive domestic resource mobilisation (DRM) through media campaigns and policy dialogues informed by studies on tax and gender and Illicit Financial Flows (IFFs). The project will especially focus on achieving reforms to strengthen property taxation in Ghana and improve revenue collection within the extractive sector in Ghana. The project will build on the successes chalked under the Fair Recovery project.</narrative>
  </description>
